---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# wiki_run_feedback: Ingest now (Index and Activity), a session's Ingest
# on Review and Me's Refresh when the wiki's one lock is held by someone
# else, and what the page says afterwards (go/tests/model/README.md).
# Its twin, wiki_check_race, is Check citations: two checks out at once
# and a result an ingest has since outdated. The flow was split there:
# together they were 5168 states and share only "an ingest landed".
#
# wiki_review models an ingest run alone and me_page one brief; neither
# has two starters meeting at .ingest.lock.
#
# Product:
#   go/plugins/wiki/run.go Run: tryLock(.ingest.lock) or `return nil`:
#     an ingest (the scheduler's tick, Ingest now, --only <session>) that
#     finds the lock held exits 0 and says nothing anywhere.
#   go/plugins/wiki/brief.go Brief: the same lock; held, it returns "an
#     ingest or brief is already running" into ingest.log and exits.
#   go/internal/serve/wiki.go wikiIngest / meRefresh answer ok as soon as
#     spawnWiki has started the process, before it reaches the lock;
#     spawnWiki counts only briefs (a.briefs, GET /api/me's `running`).
#     A holder of the lock is a headless session in the wiki dir, so
#     Activity lists an ingest or a brief as a running row.
#   go/internal/serve/web/src/wiki.tsx WikiPage: `note` and `ingestErr`
#     are WikiPage state: they live across the wiki's own screens and go
#     when the view leaves the wiki (Me is another view). Activity's note
#     is picked from activity.data.pending, the last read before the
#     click, then activity.reload(). Index's Ingest now (the Indexing
#     empty state, shown while there are no pages) sets ingestErr from a
#     failed POST and clears it only on its own next click. Review's
#     PendingRow says Started once the POST is ok.
#   go/internal/serve/web/src/me.tsx MeView refresh: a fixed 20 s
#     spinner; `running` read on reload and every 2 s while true.
#
# Fields (one Runs role):
#   screen      index | activity | review | me. The screen reads its data
#               on arrival (useLoad's key changes).
#   lock        free | ingest | brief: who holds .ingest.lock.
#   pending     a finished session waits to be ingested (the store).
#   spawn       none | ingest | session | brief: a process the page
#               started that has not reached the lock yet.
#   fate        ghost: what the last process the page started did at the
#               lock: "" (not there yet, or nothing started) | ran |
#               dropped (held; exited silently) | idle (free, nothing
#               pending) | refused (a brief that found it held).
#   seenPending the current screen's last read of `pending` (Index's
#               "N sessions are waiting", Activity's waiting count).
#   seenBusy    the current screen's last read of a run: Activity's
#               running row, Me's "Brief running".
#               A screen that does not show one holds False.
#   note        Activity's line: "" | started ("Started — the run appears
#               here in a moment.") | nothing ("Nothing is waiting…").
#   ingestErr   Index's "Ingest did not start: …" alert.
#   listed      Review lists the pending session (read on arrival only).
#   row         its button: "" | started.
#   refreshing  Me's 20 s "Writing…" spinner.
#
# Abstractions, each to keep the graph small:
# - The wiki has no pages in this flow: every run ends "No material"
#   (most do), so Index stays the Indexing empty state, which shows the
#   waiting count and not "Ingesting now". wiki_check_race has pages.
# - One process from the page at a time, and the person leaves a screen
#   only once it has settled (its reads caught up, nothing it started
#   still on the way to the lock). A second click while one is out, or a
#   move mid-flight, only multiplies paths; every interleaving at the
#   lock is still here, because the other holder is started first.
# - The scheduler's tick takes the lock only when it is free and a
#   session waits; a tick that finds it held or nothing waiting changes
#   nothing. Its own daily brief (Run's briefDue) is not modelled: every
#   brief here is Me's Refresh.
# - Every POST answers ok, except Index's Ingest now, whose POST may fail
#   (IngestIndexFails; the adapter makes ingest.log unopenable for it,
#   so spawnWiki cannot start the process).
# - A run ends (RunEnds); a brief ends (BriefEnds). Hangs are
#   runTimeout's and wiki_review's.
#
# Fairness: the processes (Reach, RunEnds, BriefEnds) and the page's own
# timers (Settle, the polls) are fair; the person, a session finishing
# and the scheduler are not.
#
# Where the mapped model was corrected against the code:
# - The Indexing state (IngestIndex's) shows neither "Ingesting now" nor
#   a run: only the waiting count. Its `ingestErr` is not cleared by a
#   later success anywhere else, and it goes when the view leaves the
#   wiki (Me), not only on its own next click.
# - The refused brief's process is counted `running` only until it
#   exits, which is at once: Me drops "Brief running" on the next 2 s
#   read and says nothing else. The spinner is the fixed 20 s.
# - The note's blindness is not only "read before the POST": the POST
#   answers before the spawned run reaches the lock, so even a fresh
#   read cannot know whether the run will ingest.
# - `note` is not cleared by leaving Activity for another wiki screen
#   (wiki_review's arrive() clears it): it is WikiPage state and comes
#   back with Activity. It goes only when the view leaves the wiki.
#
# The product does not meet the mapped claims below; they are left out
# so the check stays green, and each is spelled with the counterexample
# fizz gave when it was added (the gaps are findings, not fixed here):
#
#   StartedMeansRun  not (note == "started" and fate == "dropped")
#     Go(activity), IngestNow, SchedulerTick, Reach: the POST answered,
#     the tick took the lock before the spawned run got there, and
#     Activity says "Started — the run appears here in a moment" of a run
#     that exited at the lock. With `and lock == "brief"` added:
#     Go(me), Refresh, Reach, Go(activity), IngestNow, Reach: Ingest now
#     while Me's brief holds the lock is the same silent drop.
#   StartedMeansWork  not (note == "started" and fate == "idle")
#     Go(activity), IngestNow, SchedulerTick, RunEnds, Reach: "Started",
#     and the run found nothing waiting. The same from a stale read:
#     Go(activity), SchedulerTick, RunEnds, IngestNow, Reach (the note
#     is picked from the read before the click, which still counted the
#     session the tick had ingested).
#   RowStartedMeansRun  not (row == "started" and fate == "dropped")
#     Go(review), IngestSession, SchedulerTick, Reach: the row says
#     Started and the --only run was dropped at the lock; the session is
#     not listed again until Review is re-entered.
#   (liveness) RefusedBriefSaid  always eventually fate != "refused"
#     Go(me), Refresh, Reach, (away and back: the spinner is gone, the
#     brief still runs) Refresh, Reach, ... BriefEnds: the second brief
#     is refused by the first and nothing on Me ever says it did not run;
#     fate stays refused until the person starts something else.
#   IngestErrClears  not (ingestErr and note != "")
#     IngestIndexFails, Go(activity), IngestNow: Activity's start went
#     through, and Index, back from Activity, still says "Ingest did not
#     start".
#
# Each claim that is here was shown to fail on a one-line mutation:
# HeldLockIsNotTaken (Reach ignoring a held lock), WikiStateStaysInTheWiki
# (Go(me) keeping the note), SpinnerOnlyOnMe (Go keeping the spinner),
# StartedRowIsListed (Go keeping the row), and the liveness claims with
# Reach, RunEnds, Settle or ActivityPoll made unfair.

SCREENS = ["index", "activity", "review", "me"]

# Me counts only the briefs this serve spawned while their process
# lives: from the spawn until the brief exits.
def meBusy(r):
    return r.spawn == "brief" or r.lock == "brief"

# The current screen's read agrees with the store.
def fresh(r):
    if r.screen == "me":
        return r.seenBusy == meBusy(r)
    if r.screen == "activity":
        return r.seenPending == r.pending and r.seenBusy == (r.lock != "free")
    if r.screen == "index":
        return r.seenPending == r.pending
    return True

role Runs:
    action Init:
        self.screen = "index"
        self.lock = "free"
        self.pending = True
        self.spawn = "none"
        self.fate = ""
        self.seenPending = True
        self.seenBusy = False
        self.note = ""
        self.ingestErr = False
        self.listed = False
        self.row = ""
        self.refreshing = False

    # The current screen reads the store: what it shows of it.
    atomic func read():
        if self.screen == "me":
            self.seenPending = False
            self.seenBusy = meBusy(self)
        elif self.screen == "review":
            self.seenPending = False
            self.seenBusy = False
        elif self.screen == "activity":
            self.seenPending = self.pending
            self.seenBusy = self.lock != "free"
        else:
            self.seenPending = self.pending
            self.seenBusy = False

    # --- the person: moving ----------------------------------------

    # A typed hash or a link. Review's list and its row are
    # WikiReviewView's; Me's spinner is MeView's; the note and the alert
    # are WikiPage's and go only when the view leaves the wiki.
    atomic action Go:
        require self.spawn == "none" and fresh(self)
        to = any [s for s in SCREENS if s != self.screen]
        self.listed = False
        self.row = ""
        self.refreshing = False
        if to == "me":
            self.note = ""
            self.ingestErr = False
        self.screen = to
        self.read()
        if to == "review":
            self.listed = self.pending

    # --- the person: starting ----------------------------------------

    # Index's Indexing state: POST /api/wiki/ingest, then index.reload().
    atomic action IngestIndex:
        require self.screen == "index" and self.spawn == "none"
        self.ingestErr = False
        self.spawn = "ingest"
        self.fate = ""
        self.read()

    # The same click with the POST failing: the alert, and no process.
    atomic action IngestIndexFails:
        require self.screen == "index" and self.spawn == "none"
        self.ingestErr = True

    # Activity's Ingest now: the note is picked from the read the page
    # already had, then Activity reads again.
    atomic action IngestNow:
        require self.screen == "activity" and self.spawn == "none"
        self.note = "started" if self.seenPending else "nothing"
        self.spawn = "ingest"
        self.fate = ""
        self.read()

    # Review's Not compiled row: POST /api/wiki/ingest {session}.
    atomic action IngestSession:
        require self.screen == "review" and self.listed and self.row == "" and self.spawn == "none"
        self.row = "started"
        self.spawn = "session"
        self.fate = ""

    # Me's Refresh: POST /api/me/refresh, then me.reload() and the 20 s
    # spinner.
    atomic action Refresh:
        require self.screen == "me" and not self.refreshing and self.spawn == "none"
        self.refreshing = True
        self.spawn = "brief"
        self.fate = ""
        self.read()

    # --- the processes -----------------------------------------------

    # The spawned process reaches .ingest.lock.
    atomic fair action Reach:
        require self.spawn != "none"
        kind = self.spawn
        self.spawn = "none"
        if self.lock != "free":
            self.fate = "refused" if kind == "brief" else "dropped"
        elif kind == "brief":
            self.lock = "brief"
            self.fate = "ran"
        elif self.pending:
            self.lock = "ingest"
            self.fate = "ran"
        else:
            self.fate = "idle"

    # The launchd tick, whenever it comes.
    atomic action SchedulerTick:
        require self.lock == "free" and self.pending
        self.lock = "ingest"

    # A session finishes and waits.
    atomic action SessionFinishes:
        require not self.pending
        self.pending = True

    # The run ingests what waited ("No material": no page here).
    atomic fair action RunEnds:
        require self.lock == "ingest"
        self.lock = "free"
        self.pending = False

    atomic fair action BriefEnds:
        require self.lock == "brief"
        self.lock = "free"

    # --- the page's own timers ---------------------------------------

    # Me's 20 s timer: the spinner stops and the page reads once more.
    atomic fair action Settle:
        require self.screen == "me" and self.refreshing
        self.refreshing = False
        self.read()

    # Activity every 5 s.
    atomic fair action ActivityPoll:
        require self.screen == "activity" and not fresh(self)
        self.read()

    # The index every 15 s.
    atomic fair action IndexPoll:
        require self.screen == "index" and not fresh(self)
        self.read()

    # Me every 30 s, every 2 s while it last read a brief running.
    atomic fair action MePoll:
        require self.screen == "me" and not fresh(self)
        self.read()

action Init:
    runs = Runs()

# The lock is taken only by a process that found it free: a dropped
# ingest or a refused brief leaves the lock with whoever had it.
transition assertion HeldLockIsNotTaken(before, after):
    if before.runs.lock != "free" and after.runs.lock != before.runs.lock:
        return after.runs.lock == "free"
    return True

# A note or an alert never follows the person out of the wiki.
always assertion WikiStateStaysInTheWiki:
    return runs.screen != "me" or (runs.note == "" and not runs.ingestErr)

# Refresh's spinner is Me's own: it is never on another screen.
always assertion SpinnerOnlyOnMe:
    return not runs.refreshing or runs.screen == "me"

# A row says Started only on the Review that listed it.
always assertion StartedRowIsListed:
    return runs.row == "" or (runs.screen == "review" and runs.listed)

# Every process the page starts reaches the lock.
always eventually assertion SpawnsReachTheLock:
    return runs.spawn == "none"

# Whoever holds the lock lets it go.
always eventually assertion LockFrees:
    return runs.lock == "free"

# Refresh's spinner stops.
always eventually assertion SpinnerStops:
    return not runs.refreshing

# After any start the page reflects the outcome: the screen's reads
# catch up with the store.
always eventually assertion PageCatchesUp:
    return fresh(runs)
